Project: Salary & Skills Analysis Dashboard (Excel)

Overview

This project analyzes the relationship between data job roles, required skills, and salary levels using Excel Pivot Tables and interactive dashboard elements.

The goal was to explore how skills demand influences salary across different data-related job titles.

Tools Used
	•	Microsoft Excel
	•	Pivot Tables
	•	Pivot Charts
	•	Slicers (Interactive Filters)
	•	Dashboard Design

Key Dashboard Features
	•	Interactive filtering by Job Title, Country, and Job Skills
	•	Scatter plot showing the relationship between Skills Required vs Median Salary
	•	Bar chart highlighting Top Skills among Data Professionals
	•	Salary comparison for the Top 10 Highest Paying Skills

Key Insights
	•	Senior data roles such as Senior Data Scientist and Senior Data Engineer command the highest salaries.
	•	Higher-paying roles typically require more technical skill sets.
	•	Skills like Python, SQL, and Tableau appear frequently in high-paying data jobs.

Skills Practiced
	•	Data aggregation using Pivot Tables
	•	Data storytelling with dashboards
	•	Interactive filtering using slicers
	•	Salary and skill trend analysis
